athacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ec1632c3b5a1a9cc6f9ea87ed45cee2f5e75c2c11649b02c1231f992a01a04" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ec1632c3b5a1a9cc6f9ea87ed45cee2f5e75c2c11649b02c1231f992a01a04" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/state.json" "file_sha256" "44ec1632c3b5a1a9cc6f9ea87ed45cee2f5e75c2c11649b02c1231f992a01a04" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "62f91bb2b44beaa89a15ad2efcf57e10f3caca4a134322cc5b5c207c67f32819" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "62f91bb2b44beaa89a15ad2efcf57e10f3caca4a134322cc5b5c207c67f32819" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "8dfb0e1abec05a5681300ea7db19a2bc47f2aee9a6476a9e46270f963567f7c6" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "8dfb0e1abec05a5681300ea7db19a2bc47f2aee9a6476a9e46270f963567f7c6" "basis" 1394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-49178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316022" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}+\\ln(2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{x}^{2}+5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+5\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+5(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{13}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11005" "field" "selection" "attri