 "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-9978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{40}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{64}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-9978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/23776e39d83f9feb926b2001b9c763298c8004cad21357433926fb8f40b1ebe7.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=2$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{32}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{32}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/0a7a32f856d63403d7125f1c6bb9acc9a5fcd182c2f7fbd3f3ebdfa42f9c9c2c.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-8$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-8{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-8\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-8(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}-16 \\\\  & =-\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{56}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-316226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-316226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{56}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/0775eb4f214e6d4c0388817e59f775d306e647779fe7fb98c856a5a1ab79cb09.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}-9$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-2{x}^{2}-9)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-9\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-0)-9(2-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{3}-18 \\\\  & =-\\frac{70}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{70}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "45"] ["math" "\\frac{29}{26}"] ["math" "\\frac{29}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{38}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{70}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-11025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{70}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-345385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/d43d7419f631b479478641ac203c6816693c68ffc40ccc1d4a8a72da0a03461a.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-345385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3/2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{x}{3}){|}_{0}^{3/2} \\\\  & =arccos\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arccos\\,(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-345385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-345385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-345385" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2}-4x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})-4(2+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{32}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-54471" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/70a4f7ef7589f303924f1c48e7b0c26cd2173960847ac660199d11ae144c0afc.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\sqrt{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\sqrt{2}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4a130bd64ead094a35f810990507a1618fedd493ae7e11ee8b375b48acfde5a"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "q-73327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c7c5cb1962844028cdebbe7b597db451c7d94e4ccb8ccd7333317074bab5880"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "d68e68f2fe6ee4b95c5578c63bec34fb47f13539dfd3c9af2bf01fc772d064a6"} {"question" "e-781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/example-781.json" "file_sha256" "d68e68f2fe6ee4b95c5578c63bec34fb47f13539dfd3c9af2bf01fc772d064a6"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "a6efe56e3aff6f9c86cb14656ff0ab25b286f207885fae756e97766591aebff5"} {"question" "e-782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040771/example-782.json" "file_sha256" "a6efe56e3aff6f9c86cb14656ff0ab25b286f207885fae756e97766591aebff5"}] "usage" {"q-316022" [] "q-49178" [] "q-54471" [] "e-781" [] "q-11005" [] "e-782" []} "basis" 1464 "retractions" [[17592186304565 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is"] [17592186286993 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186096867 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above."] [17592186304572 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above."] [17592186096502 :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)"] [17592186096503 :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093610 17592186093611 17592186093612 17592186093613 17592186093614 17592186286995 17592186304567 17592186304568 17592186304569 17592186304570 17592186304571 17592186304574 17592186304575 17592186304576 17592186304577 17592186304578] "immutable_fields" [[17592186093609 :answer-field/correct] [17592186093609 :answer-field/id] [17592186093609 :answer-field/key] [17592186093609 :answer-field/type] [17592186286994 :answer-field/correct] [17592186286994 :answer-field/id] [17592186286994 :answer-field/key] [17592186286994 :answer-field/type] [17592186304566 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304566 :answer-field/id] [17592186304566 :answer-field/key] [17592186304566 :answer-field/type] [17592186304573 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304573 :answer-field/id] [17592186304573 :answer-field/key] [17592186304573 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
